# Module 3: More Kotlin Fundamentals

This module covers intermediate Kotlin programming concepts, including
generic classes, enum classes, data classes, singleton and companion
objects, interfaces, extension properties, scope functions, and
collections.

## Activities Completed

- Created a reusable generic Question class
- Used an enum class for difficulty levels
- Used a data class to represent questions and events
- Used a companion object to track quiz progress
- Implemented an interface and progress bar
- Used the let and apply scope functions
- Stored events in a mutable list
- Filtered and grouped collection elements
- Created an extension property for event duration
